Project Structure:
      Flask_and_MongoDB_YourName/
│
├── app.py
├── data.json
├── requirements.txt
├── .env
├── .gitignore
│
├── templates/
│   ├── index.html
│   └── success.html
│
└── static/
    └── style.css

app.py contains the Flask application and routes. 
data.json contains backend JSON data used by the API route. 
templates contains the HTML pages. static contains CSS styling. 
.env stores the MongoDB connection string and is excluded from GitHub 
using .gitignore. requirements.txt contains the Python dependencies.



MongoDB Configuration:

  MongoDB Atlas was configured as the cloud database for 
  this project. A database user was created and network access 
  was configured. The MongoDB Atlas connection string was stored 
  in the .env file instead of directly writing credentials inside
  the application source code.